<section>
    <h2>Three building blocks</h2>
    <div class="card-row">
        <div class="card fragment">
            <h4>HttpClient component</h4>
            <p class="card-tag"><code>RecorderHttpClient</code></p>
            <p>Decorates the HTTP client: replays, records, or passes through.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card violet fragment">
            <h4>PHPUnit Bridge</h4>
            <p class="card-tag"><code>#[UseRecord]</code></p>
            <p>Tells which HAR file a test uses.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card amber fragment">
            <h4>When running the tests</h4>
            <p class="card-tag"><code>SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER</code></p>
            <p>Decides whether to replay or to record.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="notes">
        <p>There are three building blocks.</p>
        <p>[click] One: in the HttpClient component, RecorderHttpClient. It wraps the HTTP client. For each request, it replays, records, or lets it pass.</p>
        <p>[click] Two: in the PHPUnit Bridge, the UseRecord attribute. It says which file a test uses.</p>
        <p>[click] Three: an environment variable, SYMFONY_HTTP_RECORDER. When you run the tests, it decides: replay or record.</p>
        <p>Let's see each one.</p>
    </aside>
</section>
